### request.http

```http
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Report a lost item
POST {{baseUrl}}/report/lost-item
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Black Wallet",
  "description": "A black leather wallet containing an ID card",
  "location": "University Library",
  "dateLost": "2026-10-18"
}

### 2. Report a found item
POST {{baseUrl}}/report/found-item
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Blue Backpack",
  "description": "A blue backpack containing notebooks",
  "location": "Main Cafeteria",
  "dateFound": "2026-10-18"
}

### 3. Get all reported items
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items

### 4. Filter by type: Lost
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?type=lost

### 5. Filter by type: Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?type=found

### 6. Filter by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?name=wallet

### 7. Filter by location
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?location=University

### 8. Filter by date
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?date=2026-10-18

### 9. Filter by recovery status: not recovered
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?isRecoverd=false

### 10. Filter by recovery status: recovered
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?isRecoverd=true

### 11. Combine multiple filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?type=lost&location=University&isRecoverd=false

### 12. Test invalid type
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items?type=unknown

### 13. Get an item by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/1

### 14. Get a nonexistent item
GET {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/999

### 15. Update an item's details
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Black leather wallet containing an ID card and cash",
  "location": "University Main Hall"
}

### 16. Update a nonexistent item
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "New Location"
}

### 17. Mark an item as recovered
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/1/recover

### 18. Recover a nonexistent item
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reported-items/999/recover
```
